From a504de26a892c4c525477653d7a3039c7da858c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: netrunner <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:56:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drama3 metal: int3 routed experts (3.5 bits) in
 d3_nvfp4_up/down

A layer whose expert codes are [n, 3k/8] bytes is int3: each 16-input block is
three little-endian u16 planes (sign, hi, lo) coding the E2M1 values 0, 2, 4
and 6, under the same E4M3 block-16 scales and FP32 global as NVFP4. The
loader picks the format from the tensor header; the kernels branch on one
argument, so NVFP4 arithmetic is unchanged. The device gate runs every packed
case for both formats, and its shared-gate combine reference now accepts
either side of a BF16 rounding tie the kernel's f32 sigmoid can land on.
